# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for the SECONDO regression suite.
#
# Every entry below is a REAL finding that was measured, not a false positive.
# They are suppressed so UBSan can run with halt_on_error=1 and still fail the
# suite on anything NEW. This list is a ratchet: work it down, do not add to
# it. When a finding is fixed, delete its line and the suite will keep it fixed.
#
# Measured from a full 'run-tests.sh -tty' pass on a UBSan build, 2026-08-19.
# The count is how many test suites hit it, i.e. how much of the suite each one
# is currently costing.
#
# Format is <check>:<source file>. Note this suppresses the check for the whole
# file, not just the line named, so a fix is always better than an entry here.

# 10 suites -- AttrType's copy constructor reads insideAbove from a source that
# was default-constructed and never written (observed values include 0xBE, the
# fill byte for fresh heap).
#
# Do NOT fix this by initialising the members in AttrType(). Persistent values
# are restored by reading raw bytes over the object and then running the default
# constructor on top of them:
#
#     Flob::read((char*)elem, sizeof(DbArrayElement), ...);   // DbArray.h
#     elem = (new ((void*)elem) DbArrayElement);              // ctor runs AFTER
#
# HalfSegment(), Point() and AttrType() are all empty for exactly this reason.
# Giving any of them an initialiser overwrites data that has just been restored
# from disk. A real fix has to separate the two roles -- an explicit restore
# constructor for the placement-new sites, an initialising one for everyone else.
bool:AttrType.h

# 1 suite -- same shape one level up: Attribute's copy constructor reads
# a.del.isDefined from a default-constructed source. AttrDelete's default
# constructor documents the same constraint in a comment, and the Cast functions
# are the placement-new sites here:
#
#     CastInt( void* addr ) { return (new (addr) CcInt); }
#
# Initialising isDefined would clear the defined flag of every attribute read
# from disk.
bool:Attribute.h

# 1 suite -- third-party header, not our code
bool:librip.h

# 3 suites -- invalid KeyDataType enum value in the ordered-relation key path
enum:CompositeKey.cpp

# 1 suite -- subtracting LLONG_MIN overflows long int
signed-integer-overflow:DateTimeAlgebra.cpp

# 1 suite -- member call through a null R_Tree pointer
null:JNetwork.cpp

# 3 suites -- member call through a misaligned R_Tree pointer
alignment:NetworkAlgebra.cpp

# 1 suite -- invalid TimeType enum value
enum:DateTimeAlgebra.cpp

